<title>UK: UK grain futures ease after Thursday, Friday gains.</title>
<headline>UK grain futures ease after Thursday, Friday gains.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIFFE grain futures eased in a reaction to currency inspired rises on Thursday and Friday, traders said.</p>
<p>Active May last traded 0.75 stg lower at 95.60 stg per tonne on volume of 173 lots. Total volume was 315 lots.</p>
<p>The bulk of the business was done at the lows, they said.</p>
<p>Afternoon trading was thin and the market continued to drift down as the few shipper buyers evaporated.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
